---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

// TODO(Christine/Mike): pull real entries from the PA Skateparks research —
// name, town, and a one-line note on what makes it good for beginners.
// This table is the local-SEO anchor for the whole site, so accuracy here
// matters more than almost anything else on the page.
const skateparks = [
  { name: "Skatepark name", town: "Town", note: "Beginner-friendly note." },
  { name: "Skatepark name", town: "Town", note: "Beginner-friendly note." },
  { name: "Skatepark name", town: "Town", note: "Beginner-friendly note." },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Your First Trip to the Skatepark"
  description="What to expect, skatepark etiquette, what to bring, and a guide to skateparks near Lancaster, PA."
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Parent Resources &rsaquo; First Trip to the Skatepark</p>
      <h1>Exactly what to expect, and where to go.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A skatepark full of bigger kids doing tricks can feel intimidating.
        Here's how to walk in with a plan.
      </p>

      <h2>What to bring</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A helmet &mdash; non-negotiable, every time.</li>
        <li>Wrist guards, and knee/elbow pads for beginners.</li>
        <li>Closed-toe shoes with flat, grippy soles.</li>
        <li>Water, and sunscreen for outdoor parks.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Skatepark etiquette</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>One rider at a time</strong> on a ramp or line &mdash; wait
          your turn rather than dropping in on top of someone.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Call your line</strong> if there's any doubt about who's
          going next &mdash; a quick "go ahead" or "I'm going" avoids
          collisions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Watch before you ride</strong> new terrain &mdash; a minute
          of watching how others use a feature tells you a lot.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Give beginners room.</strong> Most skatepark communities
          are genuinely welcoming to kids who are just starting out.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Safety basics</h2>
      <p>
        Learning to fall safely is one of the first things a good instructor
        teaches &mdash; before tricks, before speed. Falling forward onto
        pads and rolling, rather than catching yourself with an outstretched
        hand, is the single biggest thing that reduces injury for beginners.
        This is exactly what we cover in a
        <a href="/programs/free-clinics">free clinic</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Skateparks near Lancaster</h2>
      <p>
        Mike has personally visited and cataloged 60+ skateparks across
        Pennsylvania. Here are a few good starting points for beginners:
      </p>

      <table class="park-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Skatepark</th>
            <th>Town</th>
            <th>Good for beginners because&hellip;</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {skateparks.map((park) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{park.name}</td>
              <td>{park.town}</td>
              <td>{park.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="todo">
        Replace the placeholder rows above with real entries from the PA
        Skateparks research &mdash; this table is the page's main local-SEO
        value, so accurate, specific local detail matters most here.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .park-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .park-table th,
  .park-table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
